\subsection{Graceful Degradation Analysis}
\label{sec:exp-degradation}

Table~\ref{tab:degradation} characterizes benchmark validity as a function of replacement rate. At 20\% replacement, Spearman $\rho = 0.93$, Cronbach's $\alpha = 0.91$, and construct coverage = 0.89---marginally acceptable. Beyond the critical threshold of 28\%, validity accelerates its decline. At 50\%, $\rho = 0.85$---ranking shifts become too large for meaningful comparison.

