\section{Supplementary Analyses}
\label{sec:supplementary}

\subsection{Item-Focused Trees}
\label{sec:exp-ift}

As a methodological alternative to categorical DIF, Item-Focused Trees (IFT) treat release date as a continuous covariate. IFT flags 520 items with AUC = 0.78, slightly higher than ETS-C (AUC = 0.76), but with higher FPR (0.07 vs.\ 0.04). The automatically learned split point (September 2023) aligns with the estimated onset of accelerated benchmark leakage. Overlap with ETS-C is 62\%, suggesting IFT captures gradual contamination patterns that binary cohort splits miss.

