\subsection{Cumulative Bayesian DIF}
\label{sec:exp-bayes}

Cumulative Bayesian DIF uses the posterior from each administration as the prior for the next. Table~\ref{tab:bayes} shows power accumulation: from 0.38 (single administration, $\delta = 1.0$) to 0.72 after four administrations, with diminishing marginal returns. FPR remains controlled at 0.06. This supports DIF as a longitudinal monitoring tool rather than a one-shot detector.

