\paragraph{Reasoning-RL: preliminary evidence.}
With only 13 reasoning-RL models in the cohort, the apparent retention (0.82) reflects dilution within a large group rather than mechanistic robustness. We report this as preliminary evidence requiring validation at larger scale.

\paragraph{Partial exploitation.}
Table~\ref{tab:partial} characterizes detection power as a function of exploitation rate $p$. At $p = 1.0$, DIF achieves TPR = 0.73. Power degrades to 0.44 at $p = 0.6$ and 0.28 at $p = 0.4$. The ensemble handoff point occurs near $p = 0.55$, where DIF and ConStat TPR converge. Below $p = 0.4$, contamination effects on rankings become negligible.

