Overlap between ConStat and DIF flags is 38\%, confirming signal orthogonality: ConStat captures per-model perturbation sensitivity while DIF captures group-level behavioral anomalies. This low overlap provides the empirical basis for ensemble complementarity.

\subsection{DVD Generation Variance Evaluation}
\label{sec:exp-dvd}

DVD detection on 12 open-weight models across 500 items yields overall AUROC = 0.56 (Table~\ref{tab:dvd}). Performance is marginally better for variant contamination (AUROC = 0.61) than verbatim (0.53), but FPR = 0.14 limits practical utility. The bimodal detection rate (18\%) is too low to distinguish memorization from non-memorization via generation variance in the MCQ setting.

\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\caption{DVD detection performance. The MCQ format inherently limits generation variance signal strength.}
